{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310862,"nonce":"ISN0wMyRQtJ82NDOxSijzmJqXbM=","title":"Tensor and QTensor graduated from compile-time @:move to runtime @:shared (Arc-backed atomic refcount) in commits c7e0ed7+2c76811+7638588. ...","message":"Tensor and QTensor are now `@:shared` (Arc-backed runtime refcounting) as of commits `c7e0ed7` (runtime ARC machinery), `2c76811` (compiler `@:shared` recognition), `7638588` (stdlib annotation swap).\n\n\nThe chronic drop-analysis bug family kept surfacing on tensor lifecycles:\n- [[bugs-addinto-rebind-clone-drop-failure]] — LlamaModel.hx:65 `var hIn = h.clone(); h = block.forward(hIn);` cannot drop to bare `h = block.forward(h)` (SIGSEGV between call return and reassign)\n- [[bugs-pool-data-flow-gap]] — pool hits=0 because activation tensors never reach `rayzor_tensor_free`\n- [[bugs-llama-8b-sigsegv-at-gen-start]] — 8B Q4_K_M crashes after `[gen] streaming` (silent EXIT=0 post-cascade-partial-fix; same root class)\n\nEach fix attempt closed one sub-shape; the next bug surfaced a new uncovered terminator/scope-exit. The structural pattern in `InsertFreePass` + `mark_escaping` + `cleanup_all_scopes` is that the compiler emits cleanup at SOME terminators but misses others.\n\n`@:shared` is essentially **runtime refcounting where the count is checked at decrement-to-zero instead of statically proved**. Tensors are perfect candidates because:\n- High-value (hot-path, expensive to leak; cheap to deep-copy is no longer the question, but cheap to Arc-clone)\n- Low alloc count per token (~3000 allocs/24-token decode → ~18000 atomics → ~72μs/decode → invisible vs matmul's 10ms/Linear)\n- Drop-bug-prone via the chronic Category-A pattern\n\nAll other classes retain strict-`@:move` from [[project-move-clone-enforced]]. This is a targeted graduation, not a wholesale replacement.\n\n\n`RayzorTensor` + `RayzorQTensor` each gained:\n- `refcount: AtomicUsize` (init=1 on every constructor)\n- `parent: *mut Raw...` (null for owning, non-null for views; bumped on view construction)\n\n`rayzor_tensor_free` / `rayzor_qtensor_free`:\n- AcqRel `fetch_sub`; only the thread that decrements 1→0 runs the actual release (pool push or direct dealloc)\n- Then cascade-decrements parent if non-null (recursive for view-of-view)\n\nNew extern symbols:\n- `rayzor_tensor_arc_clone` / `rayzor_qtensor_arc_clone` — Relaxed `fetch_add`, return same pointer, O(1)\n- `rayzor_tensor_deep_clone` / `rayzor_qtensor_deep_clone` — escape hatch preserving the prior compact-to-contiguous deep-copy body (for callers that genuinely need disjoint storage)\n\nAtomic ordering follows Boost intrusive_ptr conventions: Relaxed on increments, AcqRel on the dec-to-zero gate. No Arc cycles possible — views form a DAG (each view points at exactly one parent).\n\n\nUnder `@:shared` the analyzer no longer guarantees addInto receivers are uniquely owned. Added `debug_assert!(d.refcount.load(Acquire) == 1)` at the top of `rayzor_tensor_add_into` so debug builds trap if a future caller breaks the \"addInto on uniquely-owned\" convention. Current nue/* sites (TransformerBlock, LayerNorm, Linear) audit safe — receiver is always a freshly-produced kernel output.\n\n\n- `MemoryAnnotation::Shared` variant in TAST, parses `@:shared`\n- `TraitChecker::requires_shared` mirror of `requires_strict_move`\n- `lower_derived_clone` Tier B branch: when class is `@:shared`, route `.clone()` to `_arc_clone` instead of `_clone` (the legacy deep-copy)\n- One-line gate in `hir_to_mir.rs:~35775`: only insert into `derive_move_classes` when `@:shared` is absent — suppresses `MarkMoved` / `CheckLive` emission for shared bindings without touching the `@:move` enforcement path for non-shared classes\n- `W0030` diagnostic when `@:move` + `@:shared` co-occur (incompatible)\n- `compilation.rs` use-after-move pass short-circuits via `requires_shared`\n\n\n**Closes architecturally**:\n- LlamaModel.hx:65 rebind-after-clone — both bindings hold Arc refs; bare `h = block.forward(h)` no longer crashes\n- Pool admission gate for activation tensors — refcount→0 is now the architectural trigger\n- The chronic drop-emission bug family **for Tensor/QTensor specifically**\n\n**Does NOT close**:\n- **Operational pool wiring** — Haxe-side scope-exit drops for `Tensor` locals are not emitted by the compiler. Only one explicit `.free()` in all of nue/* (`GGUFLoader.hx:231`). Phase 5 of workflow `wqkkhzxsj`: pool stats `hits=0 misses=1961 pushes=0` even WITH @:shared. The decrement-to-zero never fires for activations because no one calls free on them. Needs `InsertFreePass` to learn that `@:shared` types get scope-exit drops (cheap and idempotent — just an atomic decrement; the actual release only happens at count==1).\n- Trap-stub cascade (Category B per [[bugs-trap-stub-cascade]]) — cross-module IrFunctionId resolution; separate investigation\n- test_exception flake (Category C per [[bugs-test-exception-flake]]) — `Box\u003cHaxeString\u003e` ownership at `native_stack_trace.rs:551`\n- Multi-prompt parity caveat — haiku/Hamlet diverge from llama.cpp on this build AND on main (per [[bugs-sdot-multi-prompt-validation-gap]] sampler-config issue)\n\n\n3-run mean **14.11s / 0.867 tok/s** vs ~14.4s / 0.85 tok/s baseline. Within noise; atomic overhead invisible (~5ns × ~50 atomics/token = 0.25μs/token vs 4500ms/token decode).\n\n\nAll three verifiers refuted the \"byte-for-byte llama.cpp parity preserved on all prompts\" central claim — but only because the claim was overscoped. Parity preserved on Paris (the historical regression-test prompt); haiku/Hamlet diverge on main too. Commit messages now qualify this correctly.\n\nAll three verifiers ACCEPTED the architectural correctness: atomic ordering right, view→parent cascade symmetric, no Arc cycles, bench in noise, regression clean.\n\n\n- [[project-move-clone-enforced]] — strict `@:move` for non-shared classes (b3d9968 family)\n- [[project-addinto-fused-kernel]] — addInto in-place semantics; safety contract now augmented with debug-assertion refcount trap\n- [[project-tensor-pool]] — bucket pool whose admission gate `@:shared` makes load-bearing (once `InsertFreePass` emits scope-exit drops)\n- [[bugs-pool-data-flow-gap]] — partially addressed (architectural admission fixed; operational wiring still open)\n- [[bugs-addinto-rebind-clone-drop-failure]] — architecturally closed by Arc semantics\n- [[bugs-llama-8b-sigsegv-at-gen-start]] — re-test after this commit; previously was SIGSEGV→silent-EXIT-0 after partial cascade fixes\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_shared_arc_tensors` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}